---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
  description="Learn more about Leon Lin — background, beliefs, interests, and how to connect."
  includePerson={true}
>
  <h1>About</h1>

  <!-- Bio -->
  <section class="bio">
    <p>I'm interested in how people make good decisions under uncertainty.</p>
    <p>
      That question has taken me through investment banking, public markets
      investing, large technology companies, small startups, and building
      software of my own. I've worked at JPMorgan, a Tiger Cub, Uber, Dropbox,
      and early stage startups.
    </p>
    <p>
      Today, much of what I work on sits between investing, software, and
      decision systems.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Why I Write -->
  <section class="why">
    <h2>Why I Write</h2>
    <p>Writing is how I find out what I actually think.</p>
    <p>
      It helps me understand what I believe, find gaps in my reasoning, and
      retain ideas. Over time, it has also been one of the best ways I've found
      to meet interesting people and opportunities.
    </p>
    <p>
      Most of what I write is about investing, technology, risk, systems, and
      decision-making.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Building -->
  <section class="building">
    <h2>What I build</h2>
    <p>
      I tend to build tools for research, decision-making, and distribution,
      mostly because I want a better system for something I already do.
    </p>
    <p>
      This includes tools for public markets investing, software to separate
      signal from noise, and the infrastructre behind Avoid Boring People.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Beliefs -->
  <section class="beliefs">
    <h2>What I believe in</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Chase excellence in the things that matter to you.</li>
      <li>Stay curious, and open to new ideas.</li>
      <li>
        Take more calculated risk. The best opportunities are often asymmetric.
      </li>
      <li>Compare yourself only to your past self.</li>
      <li>You will fail. What matters more is what you do after that.</li>
      <li>Outcomes are noisy, focus on improving the process.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Interests -->
  <section class="interests">
    <h2>Interests</h2>
    <p>I'm drawn to things that reward mastery.</p>
    <p>
      I spend time on ballet, calisthenics, dance, flexibility, gymnastics,
      handbalancing, judo, and weightlifting. I'm also interested in art,
      chocolate, food, and wine.
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm particularly curious about what world class performers across
      different fields have in common.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Investing -->
  <section class="investing">
    <h2>Investing and advisory</h2>
    <p>
      I invest selectively in seed stage companies and other small ownership
      opportunities where I understand the economics and can contribute
      something beyond capital.
    </p>
    <p>
      I occasionally advise investors, founders, and companies when the problem
      is difficult and judgment matters more than execution.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Contact -->
  <section id="contact" class="contact">
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      The best way to reach me is <a href="mailto:contact@leonlins.com"
        >contact@leonlins.com</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm especially interested in hearing from investors, founders, builders,
      and practitioners working on something unusually ambitious or interesting.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
